WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.515
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.515 --> 00:00:02.862
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.862 --> 00:00:05.324
My one word is believe, and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:05.324 --> 00:00:08.048
will solve all of the major
problems of the world.

00:00:08.048 --> 00:00:09.344
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:09.344 --> 00:00:13.020
today's message is Be Truly Fulfilled.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.653
Over to you, Tony Robbins.

00:00:14.653 --> 00:00:16.514
(rooster crows)

00:00:16.514 --> 00:00:19.472
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:19.472 --> 00:00:22.283
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:22.283 --> 00:00:26.309
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:26.309 --> 00:00:28.152
- Michael Gerber, the guy
that wrote the E-Myths,

00:00:28.152 --> 00:00:29.951
you know it talks about
why so many businesses,

00:00:29.951 --> 00:00:32.615
young businesses, fail and
one of the things he says

00:00:32.615 --> 00:00:35.417
is most people are not
really entrepreneurs

00:00:35.417 --> 00:00:37.909
but they think that's what they should be.

00:00:37.909 --> 00:00:39.262
They think that's the sexy thing.

00:00:39.262 --> 00:00:40.720
That's the most attractive thing,

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.872
that's the best answer.

00:00:42.872 --> 00:00:45.319
And what I say to you is you've
got to separate the vehicle

00:00:45.319 --> 00:00:47.210
from the outcome.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:49.324
What is it that's going
to truly fulfill you?

00:00:49.324 --> 00:00:51.950
What is it that's going to give
you that extraordinary life?

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:54.766
What's going to make things
magnificent on your terms?

00:00:54.766 --> 00:00:55.946
Not somebody else's terms.

00:00:55.946 --> 00:00:58.234
Not your father, your
mother, your background.

00:00:58.234 --> 00:00:59.697
What is that really?

00:00:59.697 --> 00:01:01.099
Separate the vehicle,
because there's many ways

00:01:01.099 --> 00:01:02.313
to get to that vehicle.

00:01:02.313 --> 00:01:04.316
But I'm saying, sometimes
you got to reevaluate

00:01:04.316 --> 00:01:06.092
what's going to really make you fulfilled.

00:01:06.092 --> 00:01:07.639
What is your gift?

00:01:07.639 --> 00:01:08.739
Are you an artist?

00:01:08.739 --> 00:01:10.903
Are you the talent that
can produce something

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:12.253
no one else produces?

00:01:12.253 --> 00:01:15.699
A skill, or product, or a
service, or some impact?

00:01:15.699 --> 00:01:18.587
Are you incredibly good at management?

00:01:18.587 --> 00:01:21.602
You really know how to
manage or lead people?

00:01:21.602 --> 00:01:23.366
Are you an extraordinary entrepreneur

00:01:23.366 --> 00:01:27.086
that can take that
gigantic gut load of risk?

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:29.783
And can create the vision
and attract the talent

00:01:29.783 --> 00:01:32.376
that you need and the
managers and leaders?

00:01:32.376 --> 00:01:34.478
You may have all three abilities,

00:01:34.478 --> 00:01:37.358
but which one really fulfills you the most

00:01:37.358 --> 00:01:39.509
is going to be the critical question.

00:01:39.509 --> 00:01:40.667
Cause we tend to want to do them all,

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.037
especially in a room like this.

00:01:42.037 --> 00:01:43.323
Cause you're all overachievers, right?

00:01:43.323 --> 00:01:44.156
Me, too.

00:01:44.156 --> 00:01:45.663
And you say I can do all these.

00:01:45.663 --> 00:01:50.107
Yes you can, but what will it
do to your quality of life?

00:01:50.107 --> 00:01:52.763
See again, the secret's going to be this.

00:01:52.763 --> 00:01:56.468
What is an extraordinary
life on your terms today?

00:01:56.468 --> 00:01:58.690
Getting clear about that,
at this stage of life,

00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:00.836
where you are, where you want to go.

00:02:00.836 --> 00:02:02.207
- I think it's really
important to build a life

00:02:02.207 --> 00:02:05.259
that you are running towards
instead of running away

00:02:05.259 --> 00:02:07.203
from something that you don't like.

00:02:07.203 --> 00:02:08.246
Let me explain.

00:02:08.246 --> 00:02:11.007
I think people are hard
wired to avoid pain

00:02:11.007 --> 00:02:13.420
more than to go out and seek pleasure.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:15.370
There's been tons of studies
that have talked about it.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:16.533
People don't like pain.

00:02:16.533 --> 00:02:18.437
We love pleasure, but we hate pain

00:02:18.437 --> 00:02:19.854
more than we love pleasure.

00:02:19.854 --> 00:02:22.965
And so how that often
translates into entrepreneurship

00:02:22.965 --> 00:02:26.507
is people are acting not
out of a desire to go off

00:02:26.507 --> 00:02:28.945
and do something big and impactful,

00:02:28.945 --> 00:02:32.252
but out of fear of pain and
trying to reduce the pain

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.887
as much as possible.

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.452
I've talked to so many
entrepreneurs and I asked them,

00:02:35.452 --> 00:02:36.503
"Why did you start this business?

00:02:36.503 --> 00:02:37.502
"Why is it so important to you?

00:02:37.502 --> 00:02:39.413
"What's the reason behind it?"

00:02:39.413 --> 00:02:40.757
And whenever I get an answer like,

00:02:40.757 --> 00:02:42.774
"I really hated my last job.

00:02:42.774 --> 00:02:45.452
"My boss was really terrible.

00:02:45.452 --> 00:02:49.795
"I just wanted freedom and
I need to set my own hours."

00:02:49.795 --> 00:02:51.700
If that's why you're
starting the business,

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:53.311
you're going to fail.

00:02:53.311 --> 00:02:55.583
Cause you're just running
away from a painful life

00:02:55.583 --> 00:02:57.758
and you think entrepreneurship
is the answer.

00:02:57.758 --> 00:03:00.046
And those are not the
successful entrepreneurs.

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:01.831
The successful entrepreneurs are the ones

00:03:01.831 --> 00:03:04.199
who are going to embrace
the pain that comes along

00:03:04.199 --> 00:03:06.659
with building the business,
and they want the pleasure

00:03:06.659 --> 00:03:08.063
so much of going off and building

00:03:08.063 --> 00:03:09.892
this really important thing.

00:03:09.892 --> 00:03:12.475
Every time I make a video on YouTube,

00:03:12.475 --> 00:03:14.596
there's a lot of pain associated with it.

00:03:14.596 --> 00:03:16.568
There's comments that come
in that may not be great.

00:03:16.568 --> 00:03:18.525
There's work to come out research it

00:03:18.525 --> 00:03:20.835
and make this happen for you guys.

00:03:20.835 --> 00:03:23.910
But we push through it, because
I want to have an impact.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:26.523
Cause I want the work that I do to matter.

00:03:26.523 --> 00:03:29.538
And so I would examine
your reasons for wanting

00:03:29.538 --> 00:03:32.949
to make that change in your
life or in your business.

00:03:32.949 --> 00:03:34.893
Ask yourself why am I doing it.

00:03:34.893 --> 00:03:37.847
If it's just to avoid something
and run away from a life

00:03:37.847 --> 00:03:40.332
that you don't like,
that's not the answer.

00:03:40.332 --> 00:03:44.408
You've got to run toward
something that you're in love with

00:03:44.408 --> 00:03:48.893
and you want to build and
you want to see come to life.

00:03:48.893 --> 00:03:51.165
Stop running away from your problems,

00:03:51.165 --> 00:03:53.504
and go build something that means it.

00:03:53.504 --> 00:03:55.363
So the question today is, I'm curious.

00:03:55.363 --> 00:03:56.558
Which one are you?

00:03:56.558 --> 00:03:57.891
Did you start your business to run away

00:03:57.891 --> 00:03:59.745
from problems you had in your life?

00:03:59.745 --> 00:04:02.131
Or are you trying to build
something for the future?

00:04:02.131 --> 00:04:03.137
Really curious to find out.

00:04:03.137 --> 00:04:04.665
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:04:04.665 --> 00:04:06.511
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Tim Miller.

00:04:06.511 --> 00:04:08.553
Tim, thank you so much
for picking up a copy

00:04:08.553 --> 00:04:10.344
of my book, Your One Word.

00:04:10.344 --> 00:04:11.794
I really really appreciate it, man,

00:04:11.794 --> 00:04:13.187
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:04:13.187 --> 00:04:14.417
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:04:14.417 --> 00:04:15.685
I believe in you.

00:04:15.685 --> 00:04:17.583
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:04:17.583 --> 00:04:19.705
and whatever your one word is.

00:04:19.705 --> 00:04:21.264
And I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:04:21.264 --> 00:04:23.782
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:04:23.782 --> 00:04:26.371
♫ I wake up every morning

00:04:26.371 --> 00:04:29.788
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:04:33.044 --> 00:04:36.383
- Can we, help us appreciate
this early experience,

00:04:36.383 --> 00:04:39.594
these lean years, these
very difficult years

00:04:39.594 --> 00:04:42.419
leading up to the ultimate prize.

00:04:42.419 --> 00:04:44.002
- There is no prize

00:04:45.381 --> 00:04:46.214
out there.

00:04:47.157 --> 00:04:51.531
The only prize is this
one and what you feel,

00:04:51.531 --> 00:04:54.612
and what you want to accomplish.

00:04:54.612 --> 00:04:56.530
And if you can,

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:57.857
as you start out,

00:04:57.857 --> 00:05:00.420
these what could be lean years

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.253
or could be fat years.

00:05:05.484 --> 00:05:10.141
I feel that I very often
watch a lot of young people

00:05:10.141 --> 00:05:11.994
sort of meander around

00:05:11.994 --> 00:05:16.350
without any idea about why
they're doing what they're doing.

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:19.350
I mean to want, and to be ambitious,

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:23.936
and to want to be
successful is not enough.

00:05:25.214 --> 00:05:26.797
That's just desire.

00:05:27.824 --> 00:05:31.991
To know what you want, to
understand why you're doing it,

00:05:33.096 --> 00:05:37.179
to dedicate every breath
in your body to achieve.

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:44.399
If you feel you have
something to give, if you feel

00:05:44.399 --> 00:05:48.831
that your particular
talent is worth developing,

00:05:48.831 --> 00:05:50.656
is worth caring for,

00:05:50.656 --> 00:05:53.304
then there's nothing you can't achieve.

00:05:53.304 --> 00:05:56.220
- [Audience Member] How would
you describe fulfillment

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:58.053
as a YouTube producer?

00:05:59.235 --> 00:06:01.568
- Well, I think fulfillment,

00:06:03.001 --> 00:06:04.341
fulfillment and YouTube producer are

00:06:04.341 --> 00:06:05.233
kind of two different things.

00:06:05.233 --> 00:06:07.370
I think fulfillment in
general as a film maker for me

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:09.125
comes from creating.

00:06:09.125 --> 00:06:11.558
And that's why in 2010 ...

00:06:11.558 --> 00:06:13.008
They put the soundtrack on for this story,

00:06:13.008 --> 00:06:16.836
so I'll try to make it sound nostalgic.

00:06:16.836 --> 00:06:19.281
I left the mainstream sort of universe

00:06:19.281 --> 00:06:21.652
because I wanted to create more.

00:06:21.652 --> 00:06:24.625
So for me fulfillment comes in creation

00:06:24.625 --> 00:06:27.198
and I always say that I'm
a little bit of a junkie

00:06:27.198 --> 00:06:29.538
and my drug is uploading.

00:06:29.538 --> 00:06:32.222
Because if I haven't posted
a movie in like a month

00:06:32.222 --> 00:06:35.326
or a month and a half, I get
like seriously depressed.

00:06:35.326 --> 00:06:37.255
And the only thing that makes me happy

00:06:37.255 --> 00:06:39.631
is to get a new movie out there.

00:06:39.631 --> 00:06:41.019
That answers your question, right?

00:06:41.019 --> 00:06:42.288
- [Audience Member] Yeah.

00:06:42.288 --> 00:06:43.797
- I've never really been interested

00:06:43.797 --> 00:06:45.190
in living a balanced life.

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:46.990
I think balanced people
don't change the world,

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:47.852
first of all.

00:06:47.852 --> 00:06:50.695
I think balanced people
don't really follow a dream.

00:06:50.695 --> 00:06:53.214
This doesn't mean that you
don't have responsibilities.

00:06:53.214 --> 00:06:54.646
Like to go the other part of his question,

00:06:54.646 --> 00:06:55.936
"How can you have a family?"

00:06:55.936 --> 00:06:56.911
Well sure, you can have a family.

00:06:56.911 --> 00:07:01.458
But balance is kind of
like, I feel like balance

00:07:01.458 --> 00:07:02.627
is like a made up word.

00:07:02.627 --> 00:07:05.178
It's like invented by corporations
to make their employees

00:07:05.178 --> 00:07:06.617
think that they're happy.

00:07:06.617 --> 00:07:08.613
It's like you've got this
balance, you could work

00:07:08.613 --> 00:07:10.990
at Microsoft or something here in Seattle.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:12.490
- [Chase] There's like 10 Microsoft people

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:13.323
in the audience.

00:07:13.323 --> 00:07:14.515
- That's right, no
disrespect to Microsoft.

00:07:14.515 --> 00:07:15.723
Let's pick another company.

00:07:15.723 --> 00:07:16.556
Microsoft's a great company.

00:07:16.556 --> 00:07:17.597
- [Chase] One out of every
five people in Seattle

00:07:17.597 --> 00:07:18.430
works for Microsoft.

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:21.940
- That's right, and it's
like you got this thing,

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:23.253
and maybe you love your job.

00:07:23.253 --> 00:07:24.685
And if you love your job, that's great.

00:07:24.685 --> 00:07:26.889
But I hear from a lot
of dissatisfied people

00:07:26.889 --> 00:07:28.104
at some of these big companies.

00:07:28.104 --> 00:07:29.394
And they write in, "I'm reading your blog

00:07:29.394 --> 00:07:30.370
"from my cubicle.

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:33.183
"I have this good job and
I've got my health insurance.

00:07:33.183 --> 00:07:35.109
"I've got free yoga every Thursday,

00:07:35.109 --> 00:07:37.210
"but I'm not really ..."

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:38.409
- [Chase] Fulfilled.

00:07:38.409 --> 00:07:39.744
- Right, I'm not really fulfilled.

00:07:39.744 --> 00:07:40.629
So for me I guess I'm much more interested

00:07:40.629 --> 00:07:42.226
in that word: fulfilled.

00:07:42.226 --> 00:07:45.107
So how can you live a fulfilled life?

00:07:45.107 --> 00:07:47.079
You can live a fulfilled life
and still pay your bills.

00:07:47.079 --> 00:07:48.459
Lots of creative people do it.

00:07:48.459 --> 00:07:51.055
Lots of unconventional
people do it, and I would say

00:07:51.055 --> 00:07:53.413
if anything it's actually
much more common now

00:07:53.413 --> 00:07:54.412
than it used to be.

00:07:54.412 --> 00:07:59.145
When I first started
working online 15 years ago,

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:01.749
I didn't know a lot of other
people who were doing that.

00:08:01.749 --> 00:08:03.639
My friends thought I was
selling drugs or something.

00:08:03.639 --> 00:08:04.921
- [Chase] Well you were.

00:08:04.921 --> 00:08:07.888
- Well I was, or like
online gambling, whatever.

00:08:07.888 --> 00:08:10.649
Parents have no idea how the
internet works and stuff.

00:08:10.649 --> 00:08:12.574
But now it's much more common.

00:08:12.574 --> 00:08:14.698
So I don't really like
the word balanced myself.

00:08:14.698 --> 00:08:16.930
- [Chase] So what we'd like to do is

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:18.948
we want to replace the word,

00:08:18.948 --> 00:08:22.115
like living a balanced
life is not the goal.

00:08:22.115 --> 00:08:24.566
The goal is living a fulfilled life.

